1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:01,840
Cheers!

2
00:00:01,920 --> 00:00:03,320
<i>Come on, everyone! Let's drink to Khobfa!</i>

3
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:04,600
<i>Drink, drink.</i>

4
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:05,760
<i>Does Rin like you?</i>

5
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:07,080
<i>I don't know.</i>

6
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:08,440
<i>What about you?</i>

7
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:09,920
Do you like Rin?

8
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,320
<i>Remember what I told you?</i>

9
00:00:11,400 --> 00:00:12,440
<i>Whenever you're with me,</i>

10
00:00:12,520 --> 00:00:14,520
<i>all the unlucky things that happen</i>
<i>seem so small.</i>

11
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:16,640
I really mean that.

12
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:41,200
You're awake?

13
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:43,880
Hey!

14
00:00:49,840 --> 00:00:51,280
Why did you sleep so close to me?

15
00:00:51,360 --> 00:00:53,080
You were the one sprawled all over me.

16
00:00:55,080 --> 00:00:56,320
I should go take a shower.

17
00:00:56,400 --> 00:00:57,240
Wait.

18
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:04,840
What? Are you going to yell at me again?

19
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:07,200
Let me shower first.
You can yell at me after that.

20
00:01:07,840 --> 00:01:08,800
Wait.

21
00:01:09,520 --> 00:01:10,760
You passed.

22
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:14,400
Huh?

23
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,720
I'll let you stay as my roommate.

24
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:20,320
Huh? Holy shit. Seriously?

25
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:23,920
Are you in your right mind?

26
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:26,000
- Yeah.
- You're not hungover, are you?

27
00:01:27,320 --> 00:01:28,480
No.

28
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:41,680
See? I told you.

29
00:01:41,760 --> 00:01:44,480
I'm the best lucky charm ever, kid.

30
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:47,840
Stay with me, and you won't have
to worry about all that bad luck.

31
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:49,480
Okay, Little Khobfa?

32
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:50,760
I'm going to shower.

33
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:54,280
I thought you'd yell at me.

34
00:01:56,800 --> 00:01:57,840
<i>What about you?</i>

35
00:01:58,440 --> 00:01:59,400
Do you like Rin?

36
00:02:56,640 --> 00:02:57,840
You're carrying so many things.

37
00:02:57,920 --> 00:02:59,960
I have to stop by the faculty
to hand in my assignment.

38
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:01,520
I've got so much work.

39
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:12,880
<i>What about you?</i>

40
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:13,880
<i>Do you like Rin?</i>

41
00:03:13,960 --> 00:03:15,160
Thanks, dude.

42
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:17,280
Love, love.

43
00:03:27,480 --> 00:03:29,160
- What's wrong?
- Nothing.

44
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:31,920
Go. Don't you have to hurry?

45
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:33,680
Oh, right.

46
00:03:33,760 --> 00:03:36,640
If I don't make it in time,
Prof. James will kill me.

47
00:03:36,720 --> 00:03:37,760
Let's hurry.

48
00:03:38,400 --> 00:03:39,360
Yeah.

49
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:43,920
You're giving weirdly short answers.
Is something wrong?

50
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:46,560
Nothing. Just go.

51
00:03:46,640 --> 00:03:47,720
Let's go.

52
00:03:48,840 --> 00:03:50,120
Hurry up!

53
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:52,280
- Walk faster. Come on.
- Okay.

54
00:03:53,200 --> 00:03:55,880
I feel so relieved
now that I've handed it in.

55
00:03:56,480 --> 00:03:58,360
Thanks for helping me carry everything.

56
00:04:03,160 --> 00:04:04,760
- Is something wrong?
- No.

57
00:04:08,160 --> 00:04:11,800
Well, look who's in a good mood
after handing in his work.

58
00:04:11,880 --> 00:04:13,280
Hi, Khobfa.

59
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:15,600
Being roommates with my friend
must be exhausting.

60
00:04:20,320 --> 00:04:21,200
Not really.

61
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:22,920
See?

62
00:04:25,680 --> 00:04:28,600
Damn, it's hot today. I'm thirsty.

63
00:04:28,680 --> 00:04:30,040
Want me to buy you a drink?

64
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:32,040
Really?

65
00:04:32,120 --> 00:04:33,840
Awesome. I'll have--

66
00:04:33,920 --> 00:04:36,360
A less-sweet matcha latte
with oat milk, right?

67
00:04:42,680 --> 00:04:44,200
You remembered.

68
00:04:44,280 --> 00:04:45,120
Thank you.

69
00:04:58,520 --> 00:05:00,200
He even knows your usual drink.

70
00:05:00,280 --> 00:05:02,640
"A less-sweet matcha latte
with oat milk, right?"

71
00:05:02,720 --> 00:05:05,720
- So what exactly is going on…
- Between you two?

72
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:08,480
What? What do you mean? Nothing.

73
00:05:08,560 --> 00:05:09,800
- Oh, really?
- Oh, really?

74
00:05:09,880 --> 00:05:11,440
Really?

75
00:05:11,520 --> 00:05:12,720
Really?

76
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:14,640
What the hell is wrong with you guys?

77
00:05:14,720 --> 00:05:15,920
And there he goes.

78
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,680
All right.

79
00:05:17,760 --> 00:05:23,240
Our activity this semester is
a nature camp outside the province.

80
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:26,840
This year, we'll be going to Rayong.

81
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:33,480
Just so you know,
this assignment is worth 20 points.

82
00:05:33,560 --> 00:05:37,440
No absences or leaves will be allowed
without a valid reason. Understood?

83
00:05:37,520 --> 00:05:39,800
- Yes!
- Yes!

84
00:05:39,880 --> 00:05:44,440
Also, each room accommodates two people.

85
00:05:44,520 --> 00:05:45,960
You'll need to pair up

86
00:05:46,040 --> 00:05:48,720
and submit your names to me
as soon as possible. Understood?

87
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:51,600
- Yes.
- Okay. See you then.

88
00:05:51,680 --> 00:05:52,560
Goodbye.

89
00:05:52,640 --> 00:05:54,520
- Thank you.
- Bye.

90
00:05:56,280 --> 00:05:57,520
Want to sleep with me?

91
00:05:58,600 --> 00:05:59,440
What?

92
00:06:00,320 --> 00:06:04,200
Well, I mean at the camp.
Do you want to share a room with me?

93
00:06:06,840 --> 00:06:10,040
I was planning to tell the professor
I'm not going.

94
00:06:10,800 --> 00:06:11,720
I don't like crowds.

95
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:14,720
Huh? Hey, Khobfa!

96
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:16,880
The assignment is worth 20 points.

97
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:18,960
That's four whole grade levels, Khobfa!

98
00:06:20,440 --> 00:06:21,520
<i>What a bummer.</i>

99
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:23,280
Khobfa should come.

100
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:26,680
We were planning to egg him on
to do something to you.

101
00:06:26,760 --> 00:06:29,800
- Do what?
- What? Haven't you heard?

102
00:06:29,880 --> 00:06:31,920
This camp is amazing.

103
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:36,720
I heard there's even a legend about a tree
that can prove true love.

104
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:38,000
Yeah, that's right.

105
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:43,800
Apparently, soulmates
who kiss under that tree

106
00:06:43,880 --> 00:06:45,400
will last.

107
00:06:45,480 --> 00:06:49,120
Some couples who went in previous years
are still together.

108
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:50,480
Wait.

109
00:06:50,560 --> 00:06:55,000
You guys want me and Khobfa
to kiss under that tree?

110
00:06:55,080 --> 00:06:56,160
- Yes!
- Correct!

111
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:04,880
You guys are evil!

112
00:07:04,960 --> 00:07:06,720
- Let's go!
- Get back here, assholes!

113
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:07,760
Go!

114
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:23,360
A tree that tests true love, huh?

115
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:25,800
TRUE LOVE TREE: COINCIDENCE OR MIRACLE?

116
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:30,240
<i>My partner and I had broken up,</i>

117
00:07:30,320 --> 00:07:33,280
<i>but neither of us was sure</i>
<i>we had made the right decision.</i>

118
00:07:33,360 --> 00:07:35,360
<i>So we tried kissing beneath the tree.</i>

119
00:07:35,440 --> 00:07:39,040
<i>In the end, we got back together</i>
<i>and have been together for two years now.</i>

120
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:41,520
<i>We've been together for two years now.</i>

121
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:52,600
Hey!

122
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:53,960
No!

123
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,080
What are you looking at?

124
00:07:58,360 --> 00:07:59,400
Nothing.

125
00:08:01,080 --> 00:08:03,120
What? You looked pretty absorbed in it.

126
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:08,640
- Krit, Mochi!
- Seriously?

127
00:08:08,720 --> 00:08:12,120
Do you know there's no couple
hotter than you two right now?

128
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:16,080
Really? I guess Mochi
makes me feel at ease.

129
00:08:35,039 --> 00:08:37,240
Come on. Let me see.

130
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:39,120
No.

131
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:43,880
<i>Rin, about the camp…</i>

132
00:08:44,480 --> 00:08:47,440
Yeah, I understand.
You don't like crowded places.

133
00:08:48,040 --> 00:08:50,160
You're an extreme introvert, after all.

134
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:54,120
Honestly, I don't want to leave you alone,

135
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:57,720
but if I don't go, I'll lose 20 points,

136
00:08:57,800 --> 00:08:59,400
and my grades will tank.

137
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:01,000
You understand, right?

138
00:09:03,640 --> 00:09:08,160
But while I'm gone,
you have to be careful, okay?

139
00:09:08,680 --> 00:09:11,880
I'm worried that
without your lucky charm beside you,

140
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:13,440
you'll get hurt again.

141
00:09:18,240 --> 00:09:20,280
Hey, whose bag is that?

142
00:09:21,320 --> 00:09:22,280
Mine.

143
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:24,360
Where are you going?

144
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:26,280
To the camp with you.

145
00:09:27,080 --> 00:09:28,320
Seriously?

146
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:33,240
Do you still want to share a room with me?

147
00:09:36,240 --> 00:09:37,320
Of course.

148
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:40,600
I want to keep an eye on you
all the time anyway.

149
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:52,200
Come on, kiddos.

150
00:09:52,280 --> 00:09:54,680
I think changing your mind
was the right choice.

151
00:09:54,760 --> 00:09:58,120
Trust me. Staying alone in your room
wouldn't be nearly as fun as this.

152
00:09:59,680 --> 00:10:00,840
Yeah.

153
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:04,040
So why did you change your mind?

154
00:10:05,280 --> 00:10:07,680
Going to camp is basically a vacation.

155
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:11,920
Besides, I've never been to Rayong.

156
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,160
Aw, man.

157
00:10:13,240 --> 00:10:16,960
I thought you were so attached to me
that you couldn't stand being apart.

158
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:24,960
You're acting suspicious.
You won't even look me in the eye.

159
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:28,600
Hey, don't tell me you changed your mind

160
00:10:28,680 --> 00:10:31,640
because you want to prove your true love
under that legendary tree.

161
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:34,600
Come on! Who is it?
Got your eye on someone?

162
00:10:36,240 --> 00:10:37,720
Nonsense!

163
00:10:37,800 --> 00:10:40,960
Hey! Come on, tell me! Seriously!

164
00:10:41,040 --> 00:10:42,400
Your names, please?

165
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:44,240
- Khobfa and Rin.
- Okay.

166
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:46,600
I'll put your bag away for you.

167
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:55,200
Rin is really stubborn.

168
00:10:55,800 --> 00:10:58,720
Khobfa didn't want to come,
but he managed to bring him along.

169
00:10:59,320 --> 00:11:02,280
Maybe this isn't about making you jealous.
Something feels fishy.

170
00:11:02,360 --> 00:11:03,760
I don't think so.

171
00:11:03,840 --> 00:11:05,760
Once Rin finds out, he'll stop.

172
00:11:27,080 --> 00:11:30,840
Shit, I forgot my neck pillow.

173
00:11:31,480 --> 00:11:32,640
Are you okay?

174
00:11:33,880 --> 00:11:36,200
Yeah, I'm fine.

175
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:23,440
Hey, are you hurt?

176
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,440
What about you? Are you hurt?

177
00:12:36,200 --> 00:12:37,320
No.

178
00:12:38,520 --> 00:12:40,800
Good. Go back to sleep.

179
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:05,440
Change the song.
I don't want to listen to this anymore.

180
00:13:05,960 --> 00:13:07,360
I want some R&B.

181
00:13:08,640 --> 00:13:09,520
Here.

182
00:13:09,600 --> 00:13:11,520
No, this one.

183
00:13:19,600 --> 00:13:21,040
Hey!

184
00:13:53,280 --> 00:13:55,600
- Whoa!
- Stop!

185
00:13:55,680 --> 00:13:57,200
Khobfa, hurry up!

186
00:13:57,760 --> 00:13:59,320
What are you waiting for?

187
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:01,480
I'm soaked!

188
00:14:02,760 --> 00:14:05,760
<i>Hello to all the teachers</i>
<i>and lovely students.</i>

189
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:09,720
My name is Note. I'm an officer here
at Rayong Botanical Garden.

190
00:14:09,800 --> 00:14:11,960
- Wow.
- Welcome, everyone.

191
00:14:17,680 --> 00:14:24,400
<i>This area serves as a collection</i>
<i>of biological diversity.</i>

192
00:14:24,480 --> 00:14:27,240
<i>Most domestic plants are from the West,</i>
<i>such as the chamuang tree.</i>

193
00:14:30,120 --> 00:14:33,520
- Why are you guys in such a hurry?
- We've got a report to do!

194
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:41,640
Have you hiked through a forest like this?

195
00:14:43,160 --> 00:14:44,720
Yeah.

196
00:14:44,800 --> 00:14:47,840
When I was little,
I used to go hiking with my parents.

197
00:14:50,560 --> 00:14:53,040
That's nice. This is my first time.

198
00:14:54,720 --> 00:14:55,840
Really?

199
00:14:59,600 --> 00:15:00,840
Hey, Khobfa.

200
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:03,360
What?

201
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:07,280
You'd better stick close to me,
the luckiest guy around,

202
00:15:07,360 --> 00:15:08,840
or you might run into more bad luck.

203
00:15:12,920 --> 00:15:16,480
But you just said you've never
hiked through a forest before.

204
00:15:16,560 --> 00:15:18,080
Can I really trust you?

205
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:22,200
Of course.

206
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,800
Lucky Rin's got you.

207
00:15:26,400 --> 00:15:27,680
Follow me, kid.

208
00:15:37,080 --> 00:15:39,560
WATCH YOUR STEP, DO NOT ENTER THIS AREA

209
00:15:42,840 --> 00:15:44,280
Wow.

210
00:15:45,160 --> 00:15:46,840
Holy shit, this view is incredible.

211
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:53,080
Whoa!

212
00:15:53,680 --> 00:15:55,040
Rin.

213
00:15:56,160 --> 00:15:57,320
I'll take this bed.

214
00:15:58,080 --> 00:15:59,080
Really?

215
00:16:00,560 --> 00:16:03,240
Thanks! Now I can lie here
and enjoy the view.

216
00:16:18,240 --> 00:16:19,280
What are you doing?

217
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:21,640
So we can sleep next to each other.

218
00:16:22,840 --> 00:16:24,720
What if you have a nightmare?

219
00:16:32,920 --> 00:16:34,560
You don't have to go that far.

220
00:16:35,160 --> 00:16:38,000
It's fine. Don't worry about it.

221
00:17:06,200 --> 00:17:08,680
Wow, the view is beautiful.

222
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:11,560
Yes, Ms. Prae. Thank you.

223
00:17:12,599 --> 00:17:14,599
It's a pleasure to work with you again.

224
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:17,359
Was that a client?

225
00:17:17,440 --> 00:17:18,800
Yeah.

226
00:17:18,880 --> 00:17:21,720
Engagement was really high,
so she wants to hire us again.

227
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:24,359
This time, she wants you
to make solo content too.

228
00:17:25,400 --> 00:17:26,480
- Really?
- Yeah.

229
00:17:27,640 --> 00:17:28,560
Hey, Krit!

230
00:17:36,560 --> 00:17:38,000
Thank you so much.

231
00:17:38,600 --> 00:17:41,920
If it weren't for you, I probably
wouldn't have tried anything new.

232
00:17:50,720 --> 00:17:52,520
Oh, sorry.

233
00:17:57,840 --> 00:17:59,680
You're already talented.

234
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:02,840
Whenever you set your mind to something,
you always pull it off.

235
00:18:03,520 --> 00:18:07,960
No. I could only do it
because you were there to support me.

236
00:18:08,040 --> 00:18:11,040
Come here. I'll give you a reward.

237
00:18:12,480 --> 00:18:14,280
- Don't be a pervert, Krit.
- Hey.

238
00:18:14,920 --> 00:18:17,080
- You've gotten violent lately.
- What?

239
00:18:17,160 --> 00:18:20,320
- So, are you taking Ms. Prae's offer?
- Of course I am!

240
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:23,480
What?

241
00:18:28,120 --> 00:18:29,000
Rin.

242
00:18:31,280 --> 00:18:34,440
Have you ever heard the legend
of the tree that proves true love?

243
00:18:39,920 --> 00:18:41,680
I think that's a little too direct.

244
00:18:48,240 --> 00:18:49,160
Rin.

245
00:18:51,560 --> 00:18:53,360
There's something I need to tell you.

246
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:54,400
There you are.

247
00:19:00,440 --> 00:19:03,080
I told you.
If you're going somewhere, tell me.

248
00:19:03,160 --> 00:19:04,920
Don't wander off alone.

249
00:19:20,400 --> 00:19:23,480
You've been acting strange today.
Is there something you want to tell me?

250
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:36,320
Rin.

251
00:19:38,840 --> 00:19:39,880
I think I--

252
00:19:39,960 --> 00:19:42,080
Shit, can't we just stay friends?

253
00:19:42,160 --> 00:19:43,440
Damn it.

254
00:19:43,520 --> 00:19:46,440
You expect me to act normal? I like you.

255
00:19:46,520 --> 00:19:47,600
I can't do that.

256
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:49,920
But I don't feel that way about you.

257
00:19:50,520 --> 00:19:53,760
I don't think we can be friends anymore.

258
00:19:57,880 --> 00:20:00,800
Damn, this camp is wild.

259
00:20:01,320 --> 00:20:04,720
Seriously, if you ever fall for someone,

260
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:07,080
find out how they feel before you confess.

261
00:20:07,160 --> 00:20:09,480
Otherwise, you would
lose a friend for nothing.

262
00:20:09,560 --> 00:20:10,440
Right?

263
00:20:14,080 --> 00:20:15,080
Yeah.

264
00:20:22,280 --> 00:20:23,280
Hey!

265
00:20:23,360 --> 00:20:26,080
The seniors are calling us
to plant trees. Let's hurry!

266
00:20:32,840 --> 00:20:34,280
<i>Damn.</i>

267
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:38,080
The sun in Rayong is brutal.

268
00:20:45,600 --> 00:20:46,440
Here.

269
00:20:48,960 --> 00:20:50,040
I brought an extra one.

270
00:20:52,840 --> 00:20:54,040
Thanks.

271
00:21:14,680 --> 00:21:16,000
Is it on straight?

272
00:21:16,080 --> 00:21:17,680
Are you messing with me?

273
00:21:19,200 --> 00:21:20,280
No.

274
00:21:31,880 --> 00:21:35,200
Hey, we have matching caps.

275
00:21:36,600 --> 00:21:38,720
Did you secretly buy it for someone?

276
00:21:39,320 --> 00:21:41,040
Got you! Who is it?

277
00:21:43,520 --> 00:21:45,320
Is it really okay for me to wear it?

278
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:48,720
Yeah. Just wear it.

279
00:21:49,960 --> 00:21:51,840
No one's going to care.

280
00:21:52,440 --> 00:21:53,920
Now go plant the tree.

281
00:22:02,600 --> 00:22:05,600
Dig like this and support it right here.

282
00:22:07,720 --> 00:22:10,320
Here. Take the shovel.

283
00:22:30,360 --> 00:22:31,840
I hope the little guy survives.

284
00:22:32,800 --> 00:22:34,080
Of course it will.

285
00:22:34,160 --> 00:22:35,880
Grow up big and strong, okay?

286
00:22:35,960 --> 00:22:37,880
Hang in there, little tree.

287
00:22:56,640 --> 00:22:58,120
Let's continue.

288
00:23:00,920 --> 00:23:03,200
We should give it a name.
What do you suggest?

289
00:23:06,080 --> 00:23:08,600
I can't think of anything. You name it.

290
00:23:08,680 --> 00:23:12,160
No way. We planted it together.
It's practically our child now.

291
00:23:14,040 --> 00:23:15,480
Come on, give me a name.

292
00:23:23,080 --> 00:23:24,960
Hey! Wait, Khobfa!

293
00:23:25,680 --> 00:23:27,320
Come back and name it!

294
00:23:29,080 --> 00:23:35,520
Guys, I think Khobfa's acting weird today.

295
00:23:35,600 --> 00:23:36,600
How so?

296
00:23:36,680 --> 00:23:39,160
Isn't he wearing
his usual blank expression?

297
00:23:40,320 --> 00:23:41,640
No, this isn't normal.

298
00:23:42,480 --> 00:23:45,080
Normally, he'd be cursing me out by now.

299
00:23:46,200 --> 00:23:48,440
But he only gives me one-word answers,

300
00:23:49,520 --> 00:23:50,880
keeps walking away from me,

301
00:23:52,120 --> 00:23:53,960
and won't look me in the eye.

302
00:23:56,960 --> 00:23:58,040
Rin, dude.

303
00:23:58,600 --> 00:24:01,280
It's this obvious,
and you still can't tell?

304
00:24:02,720 --> 00:24:04,960
Think about it.

305
00:24:06,640 --> 00:24:07,840
Wait…

306
00:24:09,520 --> 00:24:12,160
He's mad because
I messed with him this morning.

307
00:24:12,240 --> 00:24:14,800
Oh, come on! He's not mad.

308
00:24:15,400 --> 00:24:20,480
That's how people are
when they secretly like someone

309
00:24:20,560 --> 00:24:22,480
- and don't know how to act.
- Huh?

310
00:24:25,880 --> 00:24:28,960
I think the guy you brought along
to make your ex jealous

311
00:24:29,040 --> 00:24:30,600
has actually fallen for you.

312
00:24:34,160 --> 00:24:35,880
I think you guys are making this up.

313
00:24:37,200 --> 00:24:39,920
Khobfa definitely…

314
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:41,240
- likes you!
- Likes you!

315
00:24:54,880 --> 00:24:55,840
Khobfa.

316
00:24:58,840 --> 00:25:00,400
So this is where you've been hiding.

317
00:25:00,480 --> 00:25:02,240
Is something wrong?

318
00:25:04,440 --> 00:25:07,160
No. I just came out for a walk.

319
00:25:08,880 --> 00:25:09,840
Don't lie to me.

320
00:25:11,240 --> 00:25:13,560
You've been acting strange
since we got here.

321
00:25:13,640 --> 00:25:17,520
You're nice to me, but you avoid me
and won't look me in the eye.

322
00:25:17,600 --> 00:25:19,760
Did I do something
that made you uncomfortable?

323
00:25:20,760 --> 00:25:22,360
You're overthinking it.

324
00:25:23,240 --> 00:25:25,280
Come on, they're about to call us.

325
00:25:25,360 --> 00:25:27,240
You're not acting normal.

326
00:25:27,320 --> 00:25:30,680
Khobfa, is it because of me?

327
00:25:30,760 --> 00:25:32,320
Did I do something?

328
00:25:32,400 --> 00:25:34,760
If something's wrong, just tell me.

329
00:25:35,360 --> 00:25:36,560
I'm willing to change.

330
00:25:37,120 --> 00:25:39,120
Please stop running away
from me like this.

331
00:25:40,840 --> 00:25:42,320
You don't have to change.

332
00:25:43,760 --> 00:25:44,800
This isn't about you.

333
00:25:46,040 --> 00:25:47,280
What?

334
00:25:47,880 --> 00:25:50,280
If it isn't me,
then what is wrong with you?

335
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:53,200
What's going on, Khobfa? Just tell me.

336
00:25:56,200 --> 00:25:57,400
I like you, Rin.

337
00:26:03,200 --> 00:26:04,840
I think I really like you.

338
00:26:06,520 --> 00:26:07,960
Can I hit on you?

339
00:26:23,920 --> 00:26:25,160
I…

340
00:26:25,840 --> 00:26:27,240
I'm sorry.

341
00:26:28,440 --> 00:26:30,960
But I've never thought of you that way.

342
00:26:32,040 --> 00:26:32,960
I…

343
00:26:34,560 --> 00:26:35,520
I'm really sorry.

344
00:26:59,880 --> 00:27:00,880
I'll be right back.

345
00:27:11,120 --> 00:27:13,560
<i>I heard you haven't been</i>
<i>focusing on your studies.</i>

346
00:27:13,640 --> 00:27:15,440
<i>You've been too busy playing influencer.</i>

347
00:27:15,520 --> 00:27:17,000
That's not true, Dad.

348
00:27:17,080 --> 00:27:20,840
I've always taken my studies seriously.
I'm working really hard.

349
00:27:21,800 --> 00:27:24,000
I only became an influencer
to help my friend.

350
00:27:24,640 --> 00:27:26,520
Besides, it was a university activity.

351
00:27:26,600 --> 00:27:27,760
<i>Don't make excuses.</i>

352
00:27:27,840 --> 00:27:30,920
<i>You just like wasting time.</i>
<i>You've always been good for nothing.</i>

353
00:27:31,600 --> 00:27:34,040
Dad, it's not what you think.

354
00:27:34,120 --> 00:27:38,360
The university activity
is really worthwhile.

355
00:27:38,440 --> 00:27:40,640
<i>Can you even get half the grades</i>
<i>your siblings do?</i>

356
00:27:43,120 --> 00:27:44,160
Yes.

357
00:27:45,000 --> 00:27:46,480
I'll try harder.

358
00:27:50,320 --> 00:27:51,720
Are you okay?

359
00:27:54,640 --> 00:27:57,480
Yeah. It's nothing.

360
00:27:58,160 --> 00:27:59,000
Let's go.

361
00:28:01,160 --> 00:28:05,040
If you're ready to have someone
who'll listen to you without judging you,

362
00:28:06,320 --> 00:28:07,520
let me know.

363
00:28:41,680 --> 00:28:44,280
Whoa! Rin, watch out!

364
00:29:01,560 --> 00:29:04,400
Krit, thanks.

365
00:29:18,600 --> 00:29:22,560
We're going to have everyone pair up.
Are you ready?

366
00:29:22,640 --> 00:29:24,400
- Ready!
- Ready!

367
00:29:24,480 --> 00:29:26,400
Then get into pairs!

368
00:29:26,480 --> 00:29:29,200
Pair up!

369
00:29:29,280 --> 00:29:30,400
Pair up!

370
00:29:30,480 --> 00:29:32,680
Two people per pair!

371
00:29:32,760 --> 00:29:35,080
Two people!

372
00:29:35,160 --> 00:29:36,480
Two people!

373
00:29:36,560 --> 00:29:38,080
Two people per pair!

374
00:29:38,160 --> 00:29:42,560
If you've found a partner, sit down.
Okay, that leaves Rin and Khobfa.

375
00:29:42,640 --> 00:29:44,240
You two can pair up.

376
00:29:44,320 --> 00:29:46,400
Give your friends a round of applause!

377
00:29:46,480 --> 00:29:48,360
Come on.

378
00:29:48,440 --> 00:29:49,880
All right, join your partner.

379
00:29:51,480 --> 00:29:57,960
Okay. Next, our staff
will hand everyone a sheet of paper.

380
00:29:58,040 --> 00:30:00,240
Staff, go ahead.

381
00:30:06,200 --> 00:30:08,520
Ready? If you are, start!

382
00:30:08,600 --> 00:30:09,720
Go!

383
00:30:11,160 --> 00:30:12,600
Perfect!

384
00:30:18,400 --> 00:30:21,200
Congratulations to the winners
of the first round.

385
00:30:21,280 --> 00:30:23,560
Fold your paper in half again.

386
00:30:23,640 --> 00:30:24,880
That's right.

387
00:30:24,960 --> 00:30:27,440
Perfect! Second round.

388
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:29,000
Start!

389
00:30:34,520 --> 00:30:36,640
Hold on to me, or you're going to fall.

390
00:30:41,760 --> 00:30:45,920
Fold your paper in half again.

391
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:47,280
Go.

392
00:30:49,440 --> 00:30:50,360
Okay.

393
00:30:50,440 --> 00:30:53,880
If you're ready, start!

394
00:30:59,040 --> 00:31:01,080
That's fab!

395
00:31:15,120 --> 00:31:16,840
Here comes the final round.

396
00:31:16,920 --> 00:31:19,800
Supporters, cheer for the team you want.
Go ahead.

397
00:31:19,880 --> 00:31:23,920
While we're waiting,
fold your paper in half again.

398
00:31:26,160 --> 00:31:28,400
Here we go.

399
00:31:40,840 --> 00:31:46,240
Final round! If you're ready, start!

400
00:31:46,320 --> 00:31:48,400
Come on, cheer for them! Let's go.

401
00:32:00,960 --> 00:32:02,000
All right!

402
00:32:20,000 --> 00:32:21,080
Put me down right now!

403
00:32:21,160 --> 00:32:22,200
Hold still.

404
00:32:32,440 --> 00:32:35,080
You both win!

405
00:32:42,160 --> 00:32:43,520
Don't ever do that again.

406
00:32:48,880 --> 00:32:50,400
How did you pull that off?

407
00:32:50,480 --> 00:32:52,120
Great job!

408
00:32:52,200 --> 00:32:53,680
You were freaking amazing.

409
00:32:54,760 --> 00:32:55,840
What?

410
00:32:57,080 --> 00:32:59,160
Like this? Right?

411
00:32:59,240 --> 00:33:02,560
Roast chicken on the fire!

412
00:33:02,640 --> 00:33:05,480
It gets stuck on a skewer!

413
00:33:05,560 --> 00:33:07,560
Skewer the left butt!

414
00:33:09,360 --> 00:33:12,440
All right, who's holding the cabbage?

415
00:33:12,520 --> 00:33:15,160
It's our handsome Krit!

416
00:33:20,680 --> 00:33:25,280
And Krit's dare is…

417
00:33:27,080 --> 00:33:31,400
to tell the person he likes
how he feels right now!

418
00:33:33,240 --> 00:33:36,120
So who's the lucky person, Krit?

419
00:33:42,200 --> 00:33:43,560
The person I like…

420
00:33:45,240 --> 00:33:49,040
is someone
who makes me feel like I matter.

421
00:33:49,920 --> 00:33:52,960
He makes me feel that
no matter what happens,

422
00:33:53,040 --> 00:33:55,320
he'll always be by my side.

423
00:34:03,240 --> 00:34:04,280
Mochi.

424
00:34:10,639 --> 00:34:12,440
Thank you for everything.

425
00:34:13,719 --> 00:34:15,600
Ever since you've been by my side,

426
00:34:17,199 --> 00:34:20,280
you've never forced me
to do anything I didn't want to do

427
00:34:20,360 --> 00:34:23,840
or become someone I didn't want to be.

428
00:34:24,360 --> 00:34:26,600
It's not like when I'm with other people.

429
00:34:26,679 --> 00:34:31,159
<i>It's not like when I'm with other people…</i>

430
00:34:35,120 --> 00:34:38,280
Why the hell is this asshole
taking a dig at Rin?

431
00:34:39,639 --> 00:34:40,600
Bastard.

432
00:34:46,159 --> 00:34:47,040
Rin!

433
00:34:49,880 --> 00:34:50,800
Rin!

434
00:34:52,239 --> 00:34:53,400
Hey!

435
00:34:56,639 --> 00:35:00,600
Did you think Rin wouldn't feel anything
after hearing you say that?

436
00:35:01,760 --> 00:35:03,040
I wasn't talking about Rin.

437
00:35:03,800 --> 00:35:05,280
I didn't mean it like that.

438
00:35:05,880 --> 00:35:07,520
But you've already said it.

439
00:35:13,800 --> 00:35:19,160
You can compliment someone
without putting others down.

440
00:35:30,320 --> 00:35:31,240
Rin!

441
00:35:37,280 --> 00:35:38,200
Rin!

442
00:35:41,160 --> 00:35:42,000
Rin!

443
00:35:43,880 --> 00:35:45,800
Khobfa! Where's Rin?

444
00:35:46,520 --> 00:35:48,560
I didn't mean it. I came to apologize.

445
00:35:48,640 --> 00:35:50,760
I never intended to insult him.

446
00:35:51,440 --> 00:35:52,720
Rin isn't here.

447
00:35:54,880 --> 00:35:55,760
Rin?

448
00:35:56,560 --> 00:35:57,480
Rin!

449
00:35:59,280 --> 00:36:01,080
Isn't Rin here, Khobfa?

450
00:36:01,160 --> 00:36:02,960
I thought Rin was with you guys.

451
00:36:03,040 --> 00:36:04,840
No, he wasn't with us.

452
00:36:05,880 --> 00:36:07,160
Where the hell did he go?

453
00:36:08,600 --> 00:36:11,560
I called, but his phone is off.

454
00:36:15,480 --> 00:36:16,760
Oh, his battery died.

455
00:36:16,840 --> 00:36:20,560
He told me it ran out
while we were playing games earlier.

456
00:36:24,040 --> 00:36:28,400
Ohm, Jinnie, wait here.

457
00:36:28,480 --> 00:36:30,960
If Rin comes back, call me right away.

458
00:36:31,040 --> 00:36:32,320
- Okay.
- Sure.

459
00:36:33,120 --> 00:36:34,720
I'll search the other way.

460
00:36:34,800 --> 00:36:36,120
Tell us if anyone finds him.

461
00:36:36,720 --> 00:36:38,360
- Sure.
- Let's go.

462
00:36:38,440 --> 00:36:39,920
Take care of Rin for us!

463
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:41,720
<i>Ever since you've been by my side,</i>

464
00:36:41,800 --> 00:36:44,560
<i>you've never forced me</i>
<i>to do anything I didn't want to do</i>

465
00:36:44,640 --> 00:36:47,200
<i>or become someone I didn't want to be.</i>

466
00:36:47,280 --> 00:36:49,360
<i>It's not like when I'm with other people.</i>

467
00:36:54,760 --> 00:36:57,760
WATCH YOUR STEP, DO NOT ENTER THIS AREA

468
00:37:24,400 --> 00:37:26,320
WATCH YOUR STEP, DO NOT ENTER THIS AREA

469
00:37:26,400 --> 00:37:27,320
Help!

470
00:37:27,400 --> 00:37:28,320
Rin!

471
00:37:30,440 --> 00:37:31,480
Help!

472
00:37:34,640 --> 00:37:35,680
Rin!

473
00:37:43,960 --> 00:37:45,080
<i>You're a jinx.</i>

474
00:37:46,640 --> 00:37:48,760
<i>Everyone around you</i>
<i>gets dragged into your bad luck.</i>

475
00:37:49,440 --> 00:37:50,520
<i>That's what you are, a jinx.</i>

476
00:37:50,600 --> 00:37:52,680
<i>They died because of you.</i>

477
00:37:52,760 --> 00:37:54,120
<i>Don't you realize that?</i>

478
00:37:55,080 --> 00:37:57,520
<i>Why didn't you die instead, Khobfa?</i>

479
00:37:59,280 --> 00:38:00,440
<i>You freaking jinx.</i>

480
00:38:00,520 --> 00:38:03,160
<i>You bring bad luck to everyone around you.</i>

481
00:38:03,240 --> 00:38:04,720
<i>Everyone died because of you.</i>

482
00:38:05,320 --> 00:38:07,480
<i>You're a fucking jinx, Khobfa!</i>

483
00:38:18,840 --> 00:38:19,800
Help!

484
00:38:21,120 --> 00:38:22,080
Help!

485
00:38:24,640 --> 00:38:27,040
Rin, don't let anything happen to you.

486
00:38:36,320 --> 00:38:37,600
Help!

487
00:38:57,080 --> 00:38:58,360
<i>Rin!</i>

488
00:38:59,120 --> 00:39:01,520
Rin! You're awake, right?

489
00:39:01,600 --> 00:39:02,800
Rin!

490
00:39:02,880 --> 00:39:04,160
Krit.

491
00:39:08,360 --> 00:39:09,320
Hold on.

492
00:39:12,280 --> 00:39:13,280
Are you okay?

493
00:39:15,880 --> 00:39:17,200
Did you save me, Krit?

494
00:39:19,720 --> 00:39:21,480
- I thought--
- I'm sorry…

495
00:39:22,760 --> 00:39:24,600
about what happened at the campfire.

496
00:39:25,800 --> 00:39:28,280
I really wasn't talking about you.

497
00:39:29,560 --> 00:39:32,600
Rin, you're awake!

498
00:39:33,200 --> 00:39:34,800
I thought you weren't going to make it.

499
00:39:36,920 --> 00:39:39,960
Krit, thank you so much.

500
00:39:40,040 --> 00:39:41,720
If you hadn't saved Rin,

501
00:39:42,280 --> 00:39:44,360
I don't know
what would've happened to him.

502
00:39:46,200 --> 00:39:48,240
You're such a hero.

503
00:39:51,960 --> 00:39:55,600
We'll go tell the teachers and seniors,

504
00:39:55,680 --> 00:39:57,240
so everyone can stop panicking.

505
00:39:57,320 --> 00:39:58,280
Let's go.

506
00:39:59,200 --> 00:40:00,120
Wait.

507
00:40:03,320 --> 00:40:04,480
Khobfa…

508
00:40:05,960 --> 00:40:07,240
What about him?

509
00:40:08,800 --> 00:40:10,720
Does he know I'm awake?

510
00:40:16,400 --> 00:40:17,600
Actually…

511
00:40:20,840 --> 00:40:22,720
I wasn't the first person to find you.

512
00:40:23,960 --> 00:40:25,120
What did you say?

513
00:40:26,360 --> 00:40:27,800
I'm not the one…

514
00:40:29,720 --> 00:40:30,840
<i>who saved you.</i>

515
00:40:36,280 --> 00:40:37,200
Rin!

516
00:40:49,960 --> 00:40:51,360
How's Rin?

517
00:40:53,880 --> 00:40:55,320
Take Rin to the infirmary.

518
00:40:57,480 --> 00:40:58,400
Okay.

519
00:40:59,520 --> 00:41:03,160
Don't tell Rin
I was the one who found him.

520
00:41:05,520 --> 00:41:06,560
Huh?

521
00:41:07,160 --> 00:41:10,360
Tell Rin you were the one who saved him.

522
00:41:10,440 --> 00:41:11,920
Got it?

523
00:41:14,760 --> 00:41:15,760
Why?

524
00:41:39,680 --> 00:41:40,880
He said

525
00:41:42,040 --> 00:41:43,440
you would feel

526
00:41:45,240 --> 00:41:47,080
more at ease that way.

527
00:41:53,920 --> 00:41:55,520
Why did he have to go this far?

528
00:42:03,000 --> 00:42:04,000
Rin.

529
00:42:07,000 --> 00:42:08,360
Rin, where are you going?

530
00:42:16,560 --> 00:42:17,600
Khobfa!

531
00:42:24,640 --> 00:42:25,840
Where did you go?

532
00:42:45,760 --> 00:42:46,880
Khobfa!

533
00:42:47,560 --> 00:42:49,080
Khobfa, where are you?

534
00:42:52,560 --> 00:42:53,840
Khobfa!

535
00:42:55,720 --> 00:42:56,840
Khobfa!

536
00:43:16,520 --> 00:43:17,480
Khobfa!

537
00:43:46,600 --> 00:43:47,880
What's wrong?

538
00:43:49,640 --> 00:43:50,840
Look at me.

539
00:43:53,680 --> 00:43:56,240
I'm such a fucking mess.
Everything I do falls apart.

540
00:43:57,760 --> 00:44:00,240
And everyone else ends up suffering
because of me.

541
00:44:02,400 --> 00:44:05,920
Don't overthink it. Rin's safe now.

542
00:44:07,080 --> 00:44:10,240
You're wasted. That's enough.

543
00:44:15,880 --> 00:44:18,760
Yeah, I'm drunk.

544
00:44:21,720 --> 00:44:23,000
Because if I weren't,

545
00:44:24,640 --> 00:44:26,520
I'd have to face the sober truth

546
00:44:27,400 --> 00:44:29,080
that I'm completely worthless.

547
00:44:33,040 --> 00:44:34,520
Just as Dad said.

548
00:44:35,880 --> 00:44:37,320
I can't do anything right.

549
00:44:37,880 --> 00:44:39,360
I can't measure up to anyone!

550
00:44:49,880 --> 00:44:51,400
I'm such a good-for-nothing.

551
00:44:53,640 --> 00:44:55,560
I'm worthless, Mochi.

552
00:44:59,240 --> 00:45:00,920
How hard do I have to try?

553
00:45:02,520 --> 00:45:04,480
Nobody wants me.

554
00:45:05,160 --> 00:45:07,400
Nobody wants me!

555
00:45:17,760 --> 00:45:19,000
I do.

556
00:45:20,720 --> 00:45:21,800
I want you.

557
00:45:59,520 --> 00:46:01,200
Why aren't you resting?

558
00:46:04,000 --> 00:46:06,200
How can I sleep
when the person who saved me

559
00:46:06,280 --> 00:46:08,880
refuses to return to the room?

560
00:46:15,800 --> 00:46:17,560
Damn Krit.

561
00:46:17,640 --> 00:46:19,160
He can't keep a promise.

562
00:46:22,040 --> 00:46:25,760
You've been overthinking all this
because I rejected you, haven't you?

563
00:46:29,320 --> 00:46:30,440
No.

564
00:46:31,840 --> 00:46:32,880
I understand.

565
00:46:34,680 --> 00:46:35,800
I think

566
00:46:37,240 --> 00:46:39,040
it really was too soon.

567
00:46:40,440 --> 00:46:42,800
I should've been
more considerate of your feelings.

568
00:46:55,200 --> 00:46:56,320
I'm sorry.

569
00:46:59,160 --> 00:47:00,560
I really am.

570
00:47:06,960 --> 00:47:09,840
Stop looking like an abandoned puppy.

571
00:47:19,600 --> 00:47:21,360
Do you even know me well enough

572
00:47:22,760 --> 00:47:24,320
to ask me out?

573
00:47:28,320 --> 00:47:29,680
Not yet.

574
00:47:31,560 --> 00:47:33,640
That's why I asked.

575
00:47:34,920 --> 00:47:36,760
So I can get to know you better.

576
00:47:51,640 --> 00:47:54,440
But you know I just got my heart broken.

577
00:47:56,640 --> 00:47:58,720
I'm afraid I might confuse your feelings.

578
00:48:13,720 --> 00:48:14,920
Also…

579
00:48:18,560 --> 00:48:20,680
if you get to know the other sides of me,

580
00:48:23,160 --> 00:48:25,280
you might end up hating me.

581
00:48:37,720 --> 00:48:41,280
I don't know what will happen
in the future.

582
00:48:43,640 --> 00:48:45,080
All I know is that

583
00:48:46,640 --> 00:48:49,560
when I'm near you,
my heart races like crazy.

584
00:48:53,200 --> 00:48:54,760
Does yours race too?

585
00:49:01,360 --> 00:49:02,680
Well, you're handsome.

586
00:49:03,760 --> 00:49:05,200
Anyone's heart would race around you.

587
00:49:05,280 --> 00:49:06,840
That's not what I mean.

588
00:49:07,880 --> 00:49:09,560
Tell me how you really feel.

589
00:49:15,360 --> 00:49:16,520
I don't know.

590
00:49:28,840 --> 00:49:30,400
But I want to find out too.

591
00:49:42,200 --> 00:49:43,960
Do you remember

592
00:49:44,760 --> 00:49:46,800
the legend of the tree
that proves true love?

593
00:49:49,320 --> 00:49:50,680
They say that…

594
00:49:53,200 --> 00:49:55,720
if a couple kisses under this tree

595
00:49:57,440 --> 00:49:59,000
and they're meant for each other,

596
00:50:00,640 --> 00:50:01,800
they will stay together.

597
00:50:06,240 --> 00:50:07,320
Of course.

598
00:50:08,600 --> 00:50:12,000
Actually, I came to this camp
because I wanted to put it to the test.

599
00:50:12,080 --> 00:50:13,800
Do you want to try kissing me?

600
00:50:17,000 --> 00:50:18,520
Do you want to kiss me?

601
00:50:22,240 --> 00:50:23,920
After the kiss,

602
00:50:25,800 --> 00:50:27,480
we'll wait three seconds.

603
00:50:30,280 --> 00:50:32,120
Whether we feel something

604
00:50:34,160 --> 00:50:35,240
or nothing,

605
00:50:36,040 --> 00:50:37,720
we both have to say it honestly.

606
00:50:37,800 --> 00:50:39,080
No lying.

607
00:50:46,200 --> 00:50:47,080
Let's do it.

608
00:51:22,760 --> 00:51:24,080
I'm going to count now.

609
00:51:26,840 --> 00:51:27,760
Okay.

610
00:51:28,880 --> 00:51:29,800
One.

611
00:51:31,520 --> 00:51:32,480
Two.

612
00:51:34,520 --> 00:51:35,480
Three.

613
00:51:36,120 --> 00:51:37,960
- I felt something.
- I felt something.

614
00:51:52,360 --> 00:51:54,080
Thank you so much.

615
00:51:54,160 --> 00:51:56,800
I'm the one who should thank you.

616
00:52:41,880 --> 00:52:44,360
<i>Last night, I made you</i>
<i>lose your way in the woods.</i>

617
00:52:44,440 --> 00:52:47,360
This time, I'll make you fall for me.

618
00:52:47,440 --> 00:52:50,160
<i>Can I try to win Rin over?</i>
<i>I'll do everything I can for him.</i>

619
00:52:50,240 --> 00:52:52,920
But if I ever make him uncomfortable,
I'll back off.

620
00:52:53,000 --> 00:52:54,160
- No way!
- No way!

621
00:52:54,240 --> 00:52:57,560
<i>What's wrong? You've been avoiding me</i>
<i>since we got back from Rayong.</i>

622
00:52:57,640 --> 00:52:58,680
<i>What else do you want, Krit?</i>

623
00:52:58,760 --> 00:53:01,480
<i>I'm already pretending</i>
<i>to date you to fool Rin.</i>

624
00:53:01,560 --> 00:53:03,560
<i>Khobfa, I have a secret.</i>

625
00:53:03,640 --> 00:53:06,800
If you find out, you might hate me.

626
00:53:06,880 --> 00:53:10,600
<i>I promise I'll hold you tight</i>
<i>and never let you go.</i>
